WEBVTT

00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:30.116
Mobility may have played a factor,

00:01:30.116 --> 00:01:33.356
but researchers also think
that greater autonomy for women

00:01:33.356 --> 00:01:34.836
and smaller family sizes,

00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:37.316
meaning that there were just
fewer cousins to marry,

00:01:37.356 --> 00:01:38.676
also influenced the change.

00:01:38.716 --> 00:01:41.796
Though it became much less popular
on both sides of the Atlantic,

00:01:41.796 --> 00:01:44.356
it was only in the US
that it became illegal.

00:01:44.396 --> 00:01:45.596
Following the Civil War,

00:01:45.596 --> 00:01:47.796
the American government
took a greater interest

00:01:47.836 --> 00:01:49.956
in overseeing more elements of daily life,

00:01:49.996 --> 00:01:51.356
including marriage.

00:01:51.356 --> 00:01:54.796
American states began to outlaw
not only interracial marriage

00:01:54.796 --> 00:01:56.196
but cousin marriage as well.

00:01:56.196 --> 00:01:59.676
Today, 32 states either
outright ban the practice

00:01:59.676 --> 00:02:02.316
or restrict it to those
who seek genetic counseling,